WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074

2
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

3
00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.840
She looks at me every day.

4
00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.720
Mary Jane Watson.

5
00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:02.720
Oh. boy. If she only knew
how I feIt about her.

6
00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.640
But she can never know.

7
00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.120
I made a choice once to live
a life of responsibility.

8
00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.440
A life she can never be a part of.

9
00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:11.840
Who am I?

10
00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.520
I'm Spider-Man. given a job to do.

11
00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.600
And I'm Peter Parker.
and I. too. have a job.

12
00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.240
Parker. Parker!

13
00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:21.520
No. no. no. stop! Stop!

14
00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.480
Parker. you're late. man. Always late.

15
00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.440
I'm sorry. Mr. Aziz.
There was a disturbance.

16
00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.800
Another disturbance.
Always a disturbance with you.

17
00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.600
Come on. 21 minutes ago.
in comes order.

18
00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:37.200
Harmattan. Burton & Smith.
Eight extra-large deep-dish pizzas.

19
00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.200
In eight minutes. I am defauIting on
Joe's 29-minute guarantee.

20
00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.120
Then. not only am I receiving
no money for these pizzas...

21
00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.840
...but I will lose the customer forever
to Pizza Yurt.

22
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.240
Look. you are my only hope. all right?
You have to make it in time.

23
00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:53.040
Peter. you're a nice guy.
But you're just not dependable.

24
00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.200
This is your last chance.

25
00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.840
You have to go 42 blocks
in 7 1/2 minutes or your ass is fired.

26
00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.360
Go!

27
00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:26.160
Hey. what. are you stupid?

28
00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:50.240
Whoa! He stole that guy's pizzas!

29
00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.160
I'm gonna get it!

30
00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.400
Hey. you guys.
No playing in the streets.

31
00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:18.760
Yes. Mr. Spider-Man.

32
00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.640
See you.

33
00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:23.000
Way to go. Spidey!

34
00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:15.560
Pizza time.

35
00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.600
You're late.

36
00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.800
I'm not paying for those.

37
00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:44.800
Joe's 29-minute guarantee
is a promise. man.

38
00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:49.440
I know to you. Parker. a promise
means nothing. But to me. it's serious.

39
00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:51.520
It's serious to me too. Mr. Aziz.

40
00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.000
You're fired. Go.
Please. I need this job.

41
00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:56.680
You're fired.
Look. give me another chance.

42
00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:06.720
You're fired.

43
00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:09.000
Parker. hello. You're fired.
Why?

44
00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:10.600
Dogs catching Frisbees?

45
00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:12.960
Pigeons in the park?
A couple geezers playing chess?

46
00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.280
Boss.
Not now.

47
00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:17.080
The Bugle could show another side
of New York for a change.

48
00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:20.040
We got six minutes to deadline. Jonah.
We need page one.

49
00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:23.520
I don't pay you to be a sensitive artiste.
I pay you... Still not now!

50
00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:26.120
I pay you because that psycho
Spider-Man will pose for you.

51
00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:29.640
He won't let me take any more pictures.
You turned the whole city against him.

52
00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:31.280
A fact I'm very proud of.

53
00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:35.000
Get your pretty little portfolio off my
desk before I go into a diabetic coma.

54
00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:38.480
It's your wife. she lost her checkbook.
Thanks for the good news.

55
00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.720
Please. isn't there any of these shots
you can use? I need the money.

56
00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:44.840
Miss Brant. Get me a violin.

57
00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:46.680
Five minutes to deadline. Jonah.

58
00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:49.400
Run a picture of a rancid chicken.
Here's the headline:

59
00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:51.320
"Food Poisoning Scare Sweeps City."

60
00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:53.760
Some food got poisoned?
I'm a little nauseous.

61
00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:55.720
All right. Mr. Jameson.

62
00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:59.400
It stinks.
Robbie. there's your page one.

63
00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:01.160
"Masked Menace Terrorizes Town."

64
00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:02.720
I told you. he's not a menace.

65
00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:04.560
I told you...
I'll take care of it.

66
00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:06.280
I'll give you 1 50.
Three hundred.

67
00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:07.800
That's outrageous.

68
00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.920
Done. Give this to the girl.

69
00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.280
Thank you. Bye-bye.

70
00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:13.080
Hi.

71
00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:14.720
Hey. Pete.

72
00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:21.240
I don't think this covers the advance
I gave you a couple weeks ago.

73
00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.480
Right.
Sorry.

74
00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:25.840
Hey.

75
00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:27.760
Chin up. okay?

76
00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:41.760
Watch it. jerk!

77
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.800
Dr. Connors. Sorry.

78
00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.480
Where were you headed. Parker?

79
00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:56.920
To your class.

80
00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:58.840
My class is over.

81
00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:01.080
See me standing here?

82
00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:04.920
I'm sorry. I'm trying.
I wanna be here.

83
00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:06.320
Then be here.

84
00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:09.040
Look at you. Peter.

85
00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:13.760
Your grades have been steadily
declining. You're late for class.

86
00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:16.680
You always appear exhausted.

87
00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:20.040
Your paper on fusion is still overdue.

88
00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:23.200
I know. I'm planning to write it
on Dr. Otto Octavius.

89
00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:26.400
Planning is not a major
at this university.

90
00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:31.520
Octavius is a friend of mine.

91
00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.720
Better do your research. Parker.

92
00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:37.160
Get it done. or I'm failing you.

93
00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.720
Surprise!

94
00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:01.760
Well. say something.

95
00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.080
What's the occasion?

96
00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:05.720
Really. Peter. It's your birthday!

97
00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:08.920
Whether you want
to remember it or not.

98
00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:12.480
He lives in another reality.
Don't you. Pete?

99
00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.440
Hi. M.J.
Hi.

100
00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.280
Hey. buddy.
Hey.

101
00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:17.600
Long time. no see.

102
00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:21.480
So how's the play?
I read a great review.

103
00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:23.280
It's going fine. It's going good.

104
00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:24.600
She's brilliant in it.

105
00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:26.400
Harry sent me roses.

106
00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.040
So where you been. pal?
You don't return my calls.

107
00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:32.200
I've been busy.

108
00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:35.800
Taking pictures of Spider-Man?
How's the bug these days?

109
00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:37.800
The less you see of that man.
the better.

110
00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.360
Now. let's all go into the other room
and have something to eat.

111
00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:42.760
I'll get the hors d'oeuvres.

112
00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:44.880
So how are things going at Oscorp?

113
00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:47.840
They're great.
I'm head of Special Projects.

114
00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.080
We're about to make
a breakthrough on fusion.

115
00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:54.240
How lovely. Harry. Your father
would be so proud. rest his soul.

116
00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:55.640
Thank you.

117
00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:59.560
We're actually funding
one of your idols. Pete. Otto Octavius.

118
00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:02.160
I'm writing a paper on him.
You want to meet him?

119
00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:03.520
You'd introduce me?

120
00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.760
You bet. Octavius is
gonna put Oscorp on the map...

121
00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:08.880
...in a way my father
never even dreamed of.

122
00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:10.880
M.J.. could you give me a hand?

123
00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:14.680
She's waiting for you. pal.

124
00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:16.560
What do you mean?

125
00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:19.040
The way she looks at you
or doesn't look at you.

126
00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:20.960
However you want to look at it.

127
00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.320
I don't have time for girls right now.

128
00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:24.800
Why. are you dead?

129
00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:26.320
I've been kind of busy.

130
00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:28.160
Taking pictures of your friend?

131
00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:31.040
Could we get off that subject?

132
00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:34.400
I want us to be friends. Harry.
I want us to trust each other.

133
00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.120
Then be honest with me.

134
00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.880
If you knew who he was.
would you tell me?

135
00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:02.960
May.

136
00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:04.640
Oh. what. Ben?

137
00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:07.760
Wait.

138
00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:09.360
Aunt May.
Oh. my.

139
00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:14.760
Oh. Peter. Oh. for a second there.
I thought I was years ago.

140
00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.680
Everybody's gone. aren't they?

141
00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:20.760
Did they have a good time?

142
00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:22.440
I'm sure they did.

143
00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:27.880
You okay?
Of course. But you go home.

144
00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:33.400
And be careful. I don't like that
scooter thing you drive around.

145
00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.240
I'm worried about you.

146
00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:40.360
You're so alone.
And I saw the letter from the bank.

147
00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:42.960
Oh. my. You did?

148
00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:44.720
Oh. well.

149
00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:46.320
So?

150
00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:48.360
I'm a little behind.

151
00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:51.000
Everybody is.

152
00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:54.560
Anyway. I don't want
to talk about it anymore.

153
00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:58.240
I'm tired.
and you better start back home.

154
00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:02.360
Here. kiddo. Happy birthday.

155
00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:04.280
You need it more than I do.

156
00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:06.880
No. I can't take that from you.
Yes. you can!

157
00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:09.000
You can take this money from me.

158
00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:11.760
For God's sake. it's not much.
Now. take it!

159
00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:14.320
And don't you dare leave it here.

160
00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.360
Oh. I'm sorry.

161
00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.880
It's just that I miss
your uncle Ben so much.

162
00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:27.600
Can you believe that it's two years
next month since he was taken?

163
00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:31.960
I think to myself at times...

164
00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:37.200
...were I to face the one responsible
for what happened. l'd...

165
00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.160
Oh. I don't know what I'd do.

166
00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:47.920
Now...

167
00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:52.440
...you better take
the rest of your cake home.

168
00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:08.040
Hey.

169
00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:10.240
Hey. You're still here.

170
00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:12.880
I saw your billboard on Bleecker.

171
00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:16.160
Isn't it funny?
I'm really kind of embarrassed.

172
00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:20.280
Don't be. It's nice.
I get to see you every day now.

173
00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:25.080
I liked seeing you tonight. Peter.

174
00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:28.920
Oh. boy. yeah.

175
00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:32.400
"Oh. boy. yeah" what?

176
00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.320
Nothing.

177
00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:44.280
Do you want to say something?

178
00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:51.560
I...

179
00:14:57.320 --> 00:14:58.480
...was...

180
00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:02.560
...wondering if you're still
in the Village.

181
00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:13.240
You're such a mystery.

182
00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:24.840
Peter.

183
00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:27.640
What?

184
00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:34.080
Happy birthday.

185
00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:44.520
I'm seeing somebody now.

186
00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:47.360
You mean. like a boyfriend?

187
00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:50.080
Well. like I like him.

188
00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:54.400
What?

189
00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:56.720
Nothing.

190
00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:00.680
That's good. you know?
Companionship...

191
00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:03.880
May be more than that.

192
00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:06.480
More?

193
00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:08.520
I don't know.

194
00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:11.920
I'm coming to see your play
tomorrow night.

195
00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:17.720
You're coming?
I'll be there.

196
00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:20.280
Don't disappoint me.

197
00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:23.240
I won't.

198
00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:38.360
Rent.

199
00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:44.520
Hi.
Hi. What's "hi"?

200
00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:46.200
Can I spend it?

201
00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:48.720
I have a paycheck due this week
and...

202
00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:52.120
You're a month late again. Again.
I promise as soon as...

203
00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:55.600
If promises were crackers.
my daughter would be fat.

204
00:16:56.240 --> 00:17:00.520
I'm really sorry. Mr. Ditkovitch. All I got
is this 20 for the rest of the week.

205
00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:02.600
"Sorry" doesn't pay the rent.

206
00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:07.400
And don't try to sneak past me. I have
ears like a cat and eyes like a rodent.

207
00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:11.840
Thanks. Mr. Ditkovitch.
Hi. Pete.

208
00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.240
Hello?

209
00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:06.960
Rent?

210
00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:14.120
Doctor? Mr. Osborn's here.

211
00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:18.040
Nobel Prize. Otto. Nobel Prize.
And we'll all be rich.

212
00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:19.880
It's not about the prizes. Harry.

213
00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:21.800
But you need money.
You need Oscorp.

214
00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:23.160
Who do we have here?

215
00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:25.040
This is my good friend
I called you about.

216
00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:26.760
He got me through
high-school science.

217
00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.840
Peter Parker. sir.
I'm writing a paper on you for...

218
00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.360
I know what you're doing here...

219
00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:33.680
...but I don't have time
to talk to students now.

220
00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:36.360
But Oscorp pays the bills. so...

221
00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:38.800
That's why I have to take off.
Board meeting.

222
00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:42.160
But my job is done here.
Got you two geniuses together.

223
00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:46.720
Good luck tomorrow. Otto.
Nobel Prize. We'll see you in Sweden!

224
00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:50.760
Interesting fellow. your friend.

225
00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.000
I won't take much of your time.

226
00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:57.360
Now I remember you. You're Connors'
student. He tells me you're brilliant.

227
00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:00.160
He also tells me you're lazy.

228
00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:02.240
I'm trying to do better.

229
00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:05.920
Being brilliant's not enough.
young man. You have to work hard.

230
00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:09.240
Intelligence is not a privilege.
it's a gift.

231
00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:11.480
And you use it
for the good of mankind.

232
00:19:11.640 --> 00:19:13.000
You want to try it back there?

233
00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:15.280
So is that it?

234
00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:19.720
Yes. My design to initiate
and sustain fusion.

235
00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:22.880
I understand you use harmonics
of atomic frequencies.

236
00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:24.360
Sympathetic frequencies.

237
00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:26.440
Harmonic reinforcement?

238
00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:28.440
Go on.

239
00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:32.360
An exponential increase
in energy output.

240
00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:34.160
A huge amount of energy.

241
00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:38.320
Like a perpetual sun providing
renewable power for the whole world.

242
00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:41.560
Are you sure you could stabilize
the fusion reaction?

243
00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:44.920
Peter. what have we been talking
about for the last hour and a half?

244
00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:47.320
This is my life's work.

245
00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:50.680
I certainly know the consequences
of the slightest miscalculation.

246
00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:53.040
I'm sorry. I didn't mean
to question you.

247
00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:56.400
Rosie. our new friend thinks
I'm gonna blow up the city.

248
00:19:56.600 --> 00:19:58.320
You can sleep soundly tonight.

249
00:19:58.520 --> 00:20:00.200
Otto's done his homework.

250
00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:03.280
Come to the demonstration tomorrow.
and you'll see for yourself.

251
00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.840
And you need
to sleep soundly tonight. Otto.

252
00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:08.080
Did Edison sleep
before he turned on the light?

253
00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:10.760
Did Marconi sleep
before he turned on the radio?

254
00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:13.000
Did Beethoven sleep
before he wrote the 5th?

255
00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:16.280
Did Bernoulli sleep before he found
the curves of quickest descent?

256
00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:18.880
Rosie. I love this boy.

257
00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:22.640
Peter. tell us about yourself.
Do you have a girlfriend?

258
00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:25.160
Well...

259
00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:27.600
I don't really know.

260
00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:30.680
Well. shouldn't you know?
I mean. who would know?

261
00:20:30.960 --> 00:20:33.800
Leave him alone.
Maybe it's a secret love.

262
00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:35.760
Love should never be a secret.

263
00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:39.080
If you keep something as complicated
as love stored up inside...

264
00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:41.320
...gonna make you sick.

265
00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:43.680
I finally got lucky in love.

266
00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:45.120
We both did.

267
00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:48.840
But it's hardly perfect.
You have to work at it.

268
00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:52.560
I met him on the college steps.
and I knew it wasn't going to be easy.

269
00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:55.800
He was studying science.
and I was studying English literature.

270
00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:59.080
That's right. I was trying to explain
the theory of relativity.

271
00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:01.560
And Rosie was trying
to explain T.S. Eliot.

272
00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:04.720
I still don't understand
what he was talking about.

273
00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:06.040
Yes. you do.
I'm serious.

274
00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:09.600
T.S. Eliot is more complicated
than advanced science.

275
00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:13.920
But if you want to get a woman to fall
in love with you. feed her poetry.

276
00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:15.520
Poetry.

277
00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.040
Never fails.

278
00:21:22.480 --> 00:21:25.280
A tall and slender maiden
All alone upon a prairie...

279
00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:27.680
Brightest green were all her garments...

280
00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:30.160
And her hair was like the sunshine...

281
00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:33.080
Day by day he gazed upon her...

282
00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:29.560
Rent!

283
00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:33.000
Where is my money?!

284
00:22:57.600 --> 00:22:59.800
You seem jittery tonight.

285
00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:01.640
You never know who's coming.

286
00:23:16.400 --> 00:23:19.240
Ladies. five minutes. Five minutes.

287
00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:36.960
How'd you do that?

288
00:23:39.880 --> 00:23:42.120
Work out. plenty of rest.

289
00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:44.080
You know. eat your green vegetables.

290
00:23:44.920 --> 00:23:48.320
That's what my mom is always saying.
I just never actually believed her.

291
00:23:51.080 --> 00:23:52.360
Come on. Go.

292
00:23:55.160 --> 00:23:56.480
Keep it steady.

293
00:24:18.120 --> 00:24:19.520
It's a web.

294
00:24:20.600 --> 00:24:22.200
Go. Spidey. go!

295
00:24:29.880 --> 00:24:31.200
We got trouble!

296
00:24:49.040 --> 00:24:50.920
Get me down!

297
00:24:51.600 --> 00:24:54.320
I am more than content
with what Mr. Moncrieff said.

298
00:24:54.480 --> 00:24:57.600
His voice alone inspires one
with absolute credulity.

299
00:24:57.840 --> 00:24:59.840
Then you think we should
forgive them?

300
00:25:02.600 --> 00:25:04.200
Yes.

301
00:25:04.680 --> 00:25:06.120
I mean. no.

302
00:25:10.240 --> 00:25:14.360
Hey. Hey. Hey. chief.
You park there. I'm towing it.

303
00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:16.280
Whatever.

304
00:25:18.760 --> 00:25:20.320
Shoelace.

305
00:25:24.640 --> 00:25:26.160
You might want to...

306
00:25:31.400 --> 00:25:35.320
Can I help you?
Yeah. I've come to see the show.

307
00:25:35.480 --> 00:25:39.120
Oh. I'm sorry. sir. No one will be
seated after the doors are closed.

308
00:25:40.320 --> 00:25:42.560
It helps maintain the illusion.

309
00:25:43.800 --> 00:25:47.120
Miss Watson. she's a friend of mine.
She asked me to come.

310
00:25:47.200 --> 00:25:48.680
But not to come late.

311
00:25:51.040 --> 00:25:54.360
I have to see this show.
Just let me in. I'll stand in the...

312
00:26:06.720 --> 00:26:09.600
A Spider-Man
A Spider-Man...

313
00:26:09.720 --> 00:26:12.640
A-does whatever a spider can...

314
00:26:12.760 --> 00:26:15.640
A-spins a web. any size...

315
00:26:15.800 --> 00:26:18.040
Catches thieves a-just like flies...

316
00:26:18.240 --> 00:26:21.360
Look out
Here comes the Spider-Man...

317
00:26:36.560 --> 00:26:39.000
You sure you don't wanna
come tonight?

318
00:26:39.160 --> 00:26:40.480
Yeah. I'm sure.

319
00:26:40.680 --> 00:26:42.440
Okay. Call me.
I will.

320
00:26:42.600 --> 00:26:44.320
You were great tonight.
Thanks.

321
00:26:46.640 --> 00:26:49.120
May I have an autograph.
please. miss?

322
00:26:50.400 --> 00:26:51.640
What are you doing here?

323
00:27:06.200 --> 00:27:07.320
You hungry?

324
00:27:07.520 --> 00:27:08.680
Starved.

325
00:27:57.200 --> 00:27:59.120
What was that?

326
00:28:03.400 --> 00:28:05.080
Okay.

327
00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:44.480
Cool Spidey outfit.

328
00:28:46.320 --> 00:28:47.480
Thanks.

329
00:28:49.400 --> 00:28:50.560
Where'd you get it?

330
00:28:51.880 --> 00:28:53.160
I made it.

331
00:28:57.000 --> 00:28:58.480
Looks uncomfortable.

332
00:28:59.800 --> 00:29:01.840
Yeah. it gets kind of itchy.

333
00:29:04.920 --> 00:29:07.840
And it rides up in the crotch
a little bit too.

334
00:29:57.200 --> 00:29:59.760
Hi. It's me.
Sing your song at the beep.

335
00:30:00.600 --> 00:30:01.800
Hi. M.J.

336
00:30:01.920 --> 00:30:03.240
This is Peter.

337
00:30:03.720 --> 00:30:06.680
I was on my way to your show and...

338
00:30:07.920 --> 00:30:11.200
Well. I was on my bike...

339
00:30:14.120 --> 00:30:15.560
Are you there?

340
00:30:18.080 --> 00:30:20.840
I really was planning on it all day.

341
00:30:22.040 --> 00:30:23.520
And...

342
00:30:24.920 --> 00:30:27.160
...I know you predicted
I'd disappoint you.

343
00:30:27.440 --> 00:30:29.040
Bingo.

344
00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:31.600
It's amazing. isn't it?

345
00:30:32.480 --> 00:30:35.240
How complicated a simple thing...

346
00:30:36.400 --> 00:30:40.280
...Iike being someplace at 8:00
can become.

347
00:30:44.000 --> 00:30:47.720
Actually. there was
this obnoxious usher.

348
00:30:48.400 --> 00:30:51.360
Somebody has to talk
to that usher. M.J.

349
00:30:51.560 --> 00:30:53.000
Your time has expired.

350
00:30:53.200 --> 00:30:57.280
Please deposit 50 cents
for the next five minutes.

351
00:31:06.600 --> 00:31:08.600
I wanna tell you the truth.

352
00:31:10.600 --> 00:31:12.000
Here it is.

353
00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:14.560
I'm Spider-Man.

354
00:31:15.680 --> 00:31:16.960
Weird. huh?

355
00:31:18.800 --> 00:31:21.000
Now you know
why I can't be with you.

356
00:31:22.080 --> 00:31:26.560
If my enemies found out about you...

357
00:31:29.320 --> 00:31:32.400
...if you got hurt.
I could never forgive myself.

358
00:31:38.040 --> 00:31:40.840
I wish I could tell you
how I feel about you.

359
00:31:51.920 --> 00:31:53.120
Ladies and gentlemen...

360
00:31:53.320 --> 00:31:56.960
...my wife Rosie and I would like to
welcome you this afternoon.

361
00:31:57.160 --> 00:31:58.760
But first. before we start...

362
00:31:58.880 --> 00:32:03.120
...has anybody lost a large roll
of 20-dollar bills in a rubber band?

363
00:32:03.480 --> 00:32:04.960
Because we found the rubber band.

364
00:32:09.440 --> 00:32:10.840
It's a terrible joke.

365
00:32:10.960 --> 00:32:12.640
But thank you for coming.

366
00:32:12.920 --> 00:32:14.120
Today...

367
00:32:14.280 --> 00:32:18.640
...you will witness the birth
of a new fusion-based energy source.

368
00:32:18.920 --> 00:32:23.920
Safe. renewable energy
and cheap electricity for everyone.

369
00:32:25.200 --> 00:32:28.360
And now let me introduce
my assistants.

370
00:32:35.680 --> 00:32:38.560
These four actuators were
developed and programmed...

371
00:32:38.680 --> 00:32:42.040
...for the sole purpose of creating
successful fusion.

372
00:32:42.200 --> 00:32:44.600
They are impervious to heat
and magnetism.

373
00:33:27.440 --> 00:33:32.040
These smart arms are controlled
by my brain through a neural link.

374
00:33:32.680 --> 00:33:35.360
Nanowires feed directly
into my cerebellum...

375
00:33:35.560 --> 00:33:39.440
...allowing me to use these arms
to control fusion reaction...

376
00:33:39.600 --> 00:33:42.320
...in an environment
no human hand could enter.

377
00:33:42.480 --> 00:33:44.800
Doctor. if the artificial intelligence
in the arms...

378
00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:46.680
...is as advanced as you suggest...

379
00:33:46.880 --> 00:33:48.800
...couldn't that make you
vulnerable to them?

380
00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:50.200
How right you are.

381
00:33:50.360 --> 00:33:52.360
Which is why I developed
this inhibitor chip...

382
00:33:52.520 --> 00:33:54.800
...to protect
my higher brain function.

383
00:33:54.920 --> 00:33:59.200
It means I maintain control of these
arms. instead of them controlling me.

384
00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:01.800
And now on to the main event.

385
00:34:01.920 --> 00:34:03.760
Give me the blue light. Rosie.

386
00:34:22.560 --> 00:34:26.240
Precious tritium is the fuel
that makes this project go.

387
00:34:26.400 --> 00:34:29.400
There's only 25 pounds of it
on the whole planet.

388
00:34:30.040 --> 00:34:34.040
I'd like to thank Harry Osborn and
Oscorp lndustries for providing it.

389
00:34:34.240 --> 00:34:36.040
Happy to pay the bills. Otto.

390
00:34:49.320 --> 00:34:50.760
Ladies and gentlemen...

391
00:34:53.240 --> 00:34:54.960
...fasten your seat beIts.

392
00:35:13.000 --> 00:35:15.440
Doctor. we have
a successful fusion reaction.

393
00:35:20.040 --> 00:35:23.240
This is a breakthrough
beyond your father's dreams.

394
00:35:23.400 --> 00:35:24.560
Thank you.

395
00:35:24.760 --> 00:35:26.560
We're producing
a thousand-megawatt surplus.

396
00:35:33.960 --> 00:35:35.720
The power of the sun...

397
00:35:36.320 --> 00:35:38.360
...in the palm of my hand.

398
00:35:59.120 --> 00:36:01.560
Keep calm! It's only a spike!

399
00:36:01.720 --> 00:36:03.440
It'll soon stabilize!

400
00:36:08.960 --> 00:36:11.640
Ladies and gentlemen.
please clear the room.

401
00:36:17.200 --> 00:36:18.560
We have a containment breach!

402
00:36:21.080 --> 00:36:23.200
Otto. please get back!

403
00:36:24.080 --> 00:36:26.800
Shut it off. Otto! Shut it off!

404
00:36:27.120 --> 00:36:29.680
It will stabilize! It's under control!

405
00:36:29.800 --> 00:36:31.640
I'm in charge here!

406
00:36:31.800 --> 00:36:34.520
It's my money! I'm in con...

407
00:36:37.960 --> 00:36:39.880
This doesn't change anything.

408
00:36:43.040 --> 00:36:45.400
What are you doing?
Pulling the plug.

409
00:36:45.800 --> 00:36:46.920
No!

410
00:37:05.120 --> 00:37:06.600
Rosie!

411
00:37:36.000 --> 00:37:37.160
Watch it.

412
00:37:37.320 --> 00:37:38.520
That was too close.

413
00:37:38.680 --> 00:37:42.600
If he had more than a drop of tritium.
he could have destroyed the city.

414
00:37:47.800 --> 00:37:49.120
I'm ruined.

415
00:37:50.720 --> 00:37:53.120
I have nothing left.
except Spider-Man.

416
00:37:53.320 --> 00:37:54.880
He saved your life. sir.

417
00:37:55.280 --> 00:37:57.560
He humiliated me by touching me.

418
00:37:57.760 --> 00:38:00.240
The press will be here soon.
I suggest we move on.

419
00:38:00.440 --> 00:38:02.200
What was he doing here anyway?

420
00:38:18.040 --> 00:38:20.360
MoIten metal penetrated
the spinal cavity...

421
00:38:20.480 --> 00:38:22.520
...and fused the vertebrae
at muItiple points...

422
00:38:22.680 --> 00:38:25.160
...including the lamina
and the roof of the spinal column.

423
00:38:25.320 --> 00:38:27.400
We won't know the extent of
the damage until we get in there.

424
00:38:27.520 --> 00:38:30.360
I suggest we cut off these mechanical
arms. slice up the harness...

425
00:38:30.560 --> 00:38:32.880
...and. if need be.
consider a laminectomy...

426
00:38:33.000 --> 00:38:36.120
...with posterior spinal fusion
from C7-T1 to T1 2.

427
00:38:36.360 --> 00:38:37.640
We're ready. doctor.

428
00:38:40.880 --> 00:38:42.560
Anybody here take shop class?

429
00:39:23.600 --> 00:39:25.800
Help me! Help me!

430
00:40:33.920 --> 00:40:37.280
No!

431
00:41:26.640 --> 00:41:29.480
It's all over town. Robbie.
Gossip. Rumors.

432
00:41:29.560 --> 00:41:31.640
Panic in the streets. if we're lucky.

433
00:41:31.800 --> 00:41:34.520
Crazy scientist turns himself
into some kind of a monster.

434
00:41:34.680 --> 00:41:37.520
Four mechanical arms welded
right onto his body.

435
00:41:37.960 --> 00:41:42.480
Guy named Otto Octavius winds up
with eight limbs. What are the odds?

436
00:41:42.600 --> 00:41:43.800
Hoffman!

437
00:41:45.760 --> 00:41:47.160
What are we gonna call this guy?

438
00:41:47.320 --> 00:41:49.480
"Dr. Octopus."
That's crap.

439
00:41:49.640 --> 00:41:51.160
"Science Squid"?
Crap!

440
00:41:51.720 --> 00:41:53.320
"Dr. Strange."
That's pretty good.

441
00:41:54.080 --> 00:41:58.080
But it's taken.
Wait. wait! I got it. "Dr. Octopus."

442
00:41:58.880 --> 00:42:00.480
I like it.
Of course you do.

443
00:42:00.640 --> 00:42:04.240
Dr. Octopus. New villain in town.
"Doc Ock."

444
00:42:04.440 --> 00:42:06.280
Genius.
What. are you looking for a raise?

445
00:42:06.480 --> 00:42:08.080
Get out.

446
00:42:08.760 --> 00:42:10.000
Chief. I found Parker.

447
00:42:10.120 --> 00:42:12.240
Where you been?
Why don't you pay your phone bill.

448
00:42:12.400 --> 00:42:14.600
Mad scientist goes berserk.
we don't have pictures!

449
00:42:14.800 --> 00:42:16.000
I heard Spider-Man was there.

450
00:42:17.120 --> 00:42:19.560
Where were you?
Photographing squirrels? You're fired.

451
00:42:19.760 --> 00:42:21.000
Chief. the planetarium party.

452
00:42:21.160 --> 00:42:22.800
You're un-fired.
I need you. come here.

453
00:42:23.000 --> 00:42:24.480
What do you know
about high society?

454
00:42:24.720 --> 00:42:26.880
Oh. Well. l...
Don't answer that.

455
00:42:27.000 --> 00:42:30.280
My society photographer got hit in the
head by a polo ball. You're all I got.

456
00:42:30.480 --> 00:42:33.360
Big party for an American hero.
My son. the astronaut.

457
00:42:33.480 --> 00:42:35.160
Could you pay me in advance?

458
00:42:43.840 --> 00:42:46.200
You serious? Pay you for what?
Standing there?

459
00:42:46.320 --> 00:42:48.920
The planetarium. tomorrow night.
8:00. There's the door.

460
00:43:03.360 --> 00:43:05.040
My Rosie's dead.

461
00:43:07.160 --> 00:43:08.840
My dream is dead.

462
00:43:12.320 --> 00:43:13.560
And these...

463
00:43:15.480 --> 00:43:18.840
...monstrous things should be
at the bottom of the river...

464
00:43:21.560 --> 00:43:22.920
...along with me.

465
00:43:31.520 --> 00:43:33.040
Something...

466
00:43:34.480 --> 00:43:35.920
...in my head.

467
00:43:39.400 --> 00:43:40.920
Something talking.

468
00:43:44.800 --> 00:43:46.240
The inhibitor chip!

469
00:43:49.480 --> 00:43:50.960
Gone.

470
00:43:55.520 --> 00:43:56.840
Rebuild.

471
00:44:00.080 --> 00:44:01.680
No.

472
00:44:02.800 --> 00:44:04.200
Peter was right.

473
00:44:06.400 --> 00:44:07.960
I miscalculated.

474
00:44:14.240 --> 00:44:16.240
I couldn't have miscalculated.

475
00:44:17.360 --> 00:44:19.160
It was working. wasn't it?

476
00:44:23.880 --> 00:44:25.200
Yes.

477
00:44:26.200 --> 00:44:29.080
We could rebuild.
Enlarge the containment field.

478
00:44:29.280 --> 00:44:31.440
Make it bigger
and stronger than ever.

479
00:44:32.320 --> 00:44:34.040
But we need money.

480
00:44:35.760 --> 00:44:37.000
Steal it?

481
00:44:37.200 --> 00:44:38.920
No. no. no. I'm not a criminal.

482
00:44:41.480 --> 00:44:42.720
That's right.

483
00:44:44.600 --> 00:44:47.640
The real crime would be not to finish
what we started.

484
00:44:51.120 --> 00:44:52.680
We'll do it here.

485
00:44:53.400 --> 00:44:56.560
The power of the sun
in the palm of my hand.

486
00:44:56.880 --> 00:44:59.240
Nothing will stand in our way.

487
00:44:59.400 --> 00:45:00.680
Nothing!

488
00:45:05.920 --> 00:45:08.400
That's the social security.
Yes. I see.

489
00:45:08.720 --> 00:45:10.320
My uncle Ben's life insurance.

490
00:45:10.480 --> 00:45:12.640
Yes. but I'm afraid...

491
00:45:12.800 --> 00:45:15.760
...it's just not sufficient
to refinance your home.

492
00:45:16.080 --> 00:45:19.400
Oh. but I'm giving
piano lessons again.

493
00:45:19.640 --> 00:45:20.840
You are?

494
00:45:25.760 --> 00:45:28.880
We appreciate
that you've just opened up...

495
00:45:29.040 --> 00:45:31.520
...a new supersaver account
with us today.

496
00:45:31.680 --> 00:45:32.920
But the fact is...

497
00:45:33.080 --> 00:45:37.200
...you do not have the assets
to justify this loan. I'm sorry.

498
00:45:37.800 --> 00:45:39.280
Well...

499
00:45:41.040 --> 00:45:42.800
At least we get the toaster.

500
00:45:42.960 --> 00:45:46.840
Actually. that's only
with a deposit of 300 or more.

501
00:45:49.560 --> 00:45:50.800
Oh. yes. I see.

502
00:45:52.240 --> 00:45:53.760
Okay.

503
00:45:56.720 --> 00:45:58.760
Don't worry. we'll figure it out.

504
00:46:15.360 --> 00:46:16.640
Peter?

505
00:46:18.320 --> 00:46:20.240
Don't leave me.

506
00:46:21.080 --> 00:46:23.360
Oh. that boy of yours is a real hero.

507
00:46:23.840 --> 00:46:25.040
Hold it!

508
00:46:25.760 --> 00:46:28.360
Put your arms up! All of them!

509
00:46:50.680 --> 00:46:51.880
Here's your change!

510
00:47:01.480 --> 00:47:02.960
Oh. no. Come on!

511
00:47:15.760 --> 00:47:17.880
You're getting on my nerves.
I have a knack for that.

512
00:47:18.040 --> 00:47:19.560
Not anymore.

513
00:47:48.160 --> 00:47:49.840
Freeze! Don't move!
Freeze!

514
00:47:53.600 --> 00:47:55.400
Hold your fire!
Don't follow me.

515
00:47:59.080 --> 00:48:00.800
Wait a second.

516
00:48:17.760 --> 00:48:20.000
Hand her over.
Of course.

517
00:48:20.720 --> 00:48:21.920
Easy. now.

518
00:48:23.600 --> 00:48:25.160
Butterfingers.

519
00:48:36.960 --> 00:48:38.200
Look out!

520
00:48:40.320 --> 00:48:42.080
Help me!

521
00:48:44.160 --> 00:48:46.640
Help me!
I'm coming!

522
00:48:51.680 --> 00:48:53.520
Hang on!

523
00:49:10.560 --> 00:49:11.920
Help!

524
00:49:30.960 --> 00:49:32.520
Thank you.

525
00:49:35.640 --> 00:49:36.920
Aunt May.

526
00:49:37.080 --> 00:49:39.960
You've stuck your webs
in my business for the last time.

527
00:49:40.160 --> 00:49:43.040
Now you'll have this woman's death
on your conscience.

528
00:49:48.360 --> 00:49:49.960
Come on.

529
00:49:53.760 --> 00:49:55.760
Shame on you.

530
00:50:26.880 --> 00:50:28.440
There you go.

531
00:50:29.360 --> 00:50:32.560
Thank you.
Oh. have I been wrong about you.

532
00:50:32.720 --> 00:50:33.960
We sure showed him.

533
00:50:34.120 --> 00:50:35.800
What do you mean. "we"?

534
00:50:39.800 --> 00:50:42.080
Take me with you. Spider-Man.
Take me.

535
00:51:08.400 --> 00:51:10.880
May I?
Sure. Go ahead.

536
00:51:11.840 --> 00:51:13.720
Penny! Over here!

537
00:51:18.840 --> 00:51:20.280
Leave it.

538
00:51:24.160 --> 00:51:26.600
Hey. Might wanna take it easy. buddy.

539
00:51:26.760 --> 00:51:28.000
Why? It's a party.

540
00:51:28.200 --> 00:51:31.040
Wouldn't you be drinking if you lost
a bundle on some crackpot...

541
00:51:31.160 --> 00:51:34.400
...who you thought was gonna take
you with him to fame and fortune?

542
00:51:34.760 --> 00:51:36.360
Not to mention your friend the bug.

543
00:51:36.920 --> 00:51:38.080
Not tonight. Harry.

544
00:51:38.280 --> 00:51:41.560
Every night!
Until I find him. it's 24-7.

545
00:51:42.040 --> 00:51:43.440
Parker!

546
00:51:44.080 --> 00:51:45.200
Parker!

547
00:51:45.800 --> 00:51:48.680
Parker! What. are you deaf?
I called you twice.

548
00:51:48.880 --> 00:51:50.720
Think I'm paying you
to sip champagne?

549
00:51:50.960 --> 00:51:52.840
Get a shot of my wife
with the minister.

550
00:51:53.240 --> 00:51:54.440
Beautiful tie.

551
00:51:54.600 --> 00:51:56.720
Get a shot of us with the DA.

552
00:51:57.160 --> 00:51:58.600
Beautiful dress.

553
00:51:59.040 --> 00:52:01.560
Here. get a shot of the mayor
and his girlfriend.

554
00:52:02.920 --> 00:52:04.440
Wife.

555
00:52:06.320 --> 00:52:08.520
Ladies and gentlemen.
good evening.

556
00:52:08.720 --> 00:52:11.640
The committee for
the Science Library of New York...

557
00:52:11.840 --> 00:52:13.960
...is pleased to present
our guest of honor.

558
00:52:14.120 --> 00:52:17.680
He's the first man to play football
on the moon.

559
00:52:18.800 --> 00:52:21.800
The handsome. the heroic.
the delicious...

560
00:52:21.960 --> 00:52:23.760
...Captain John Jameson.

561
00:53:06.600 --> 00:53:08.080
Hi.

562
00:53:10.280 --> 00:53:13.480
You.
Listen. I'm sorry.

563
00:53:13.640 --> 00:53:15.720
But there was a disturbance.

564
00:53:15.960 --> 00:53:17.240
I don't know you.

565
00:53:19.120 --> 00:53:22.840
And I can't keep thinking about you.
It's too painful.

566
00:53:23.720 --> 00:53:25.360
I've been reading poetry lately.

567
00:53:25.520 --> 00:53:26.840
Whatever that means.

568
00:53:27.280 --> 00:53:30.720
Day by day he gazed upon her...

569
00:53:31.080 --> 00:53:33.800
Day by day he sighed with passion
Day by day...

570
00:53:33.960 --> 00:53:35.760
Don't start.

571
00:53:37.080 --> 00:53:38.760
Can I get you a drink?

572
00:53:39.000 --> 00:53:40.680
I'm with John. He'll get me my drink.

573
00:53:41.360 --> 00:53:42.880
John.

574
00:53:43.080 --> 00:53:46.840
By the way. John has seen
my show five times.

575
00:53:47.000 --> 00:53:49.840
Harry has seen it twice.
Aunt May has seen it.

576
00:53:50.000 --> 00:53:52.400
My sick mother got out of bed to see it.

577
00:53:52.600 --> 00:53:53.720
Even my father.

578
00:53:54.880 --> 00:53:57.520
He came backstage to borrow cash.

579
00:53:59.120 --> 00:54:03.280
But my best friend.
who cares so much about me...

580
00:54:03.400 --> 00:54:05.480
...can't make an 8:00 curtain.

581
00:54:07.160 --> 00:54:08.640
After all these years...

582
00:54:09.920 --> 00:54:12.400
...he's nothing to me
but an empty seat.

583
00:54:36.840 --> 00:54:40.040
It pisses me off. your loyaIty to
Spider-Man and not to your best friend.

584
00:54:40.240 --> 00:54:43.360
I find him with my father's body.
and you defend him.

585
00:54:43.520 --> 00:54:45.440
Take it easy.
Don't push me.

586
00:54:45.600 --> 00:54:47.360
Don't act like you're my friend.

587
00:54:48.160 --> 00:54:50.040
You stole M.J. from me.

588
00:54:50.320 --> 00:54:52.240
You stole my father's love.

589
00:54:52.840 --> 00:54:57.640
Then you let him die because you
didn't turn in the freak. Isn't that right?

590
00:54:58.840 --> 00:55:01.000
Huh? Isn't that right?

591
00:55:01.160 --> 00:55:02.880
Huh. brother?

592
00:55:13.440 --> 00:55:16.000
Ladies and gentlemen.
I just want you all to know...

593
00:55:16.680 --> 00:55:21.000
...that the beautiful Miss Mary Jane
Watson has just agreed to marry me.

594
00:55:31.080 --> 00:55:32.520
What a surprise.

595
00:55:32.640 --> 00:55:35.400
Parker. wake up! Wake up!
Shoot the picture!

596
00:56:01.440 --> 00:56:03.600
Oh. no. No!

597
00:56:14.240 --> 00:56:16.280
Why is this happening to me?

598
00:57:40.080 --> 00:57:41.920
You seem very okay to me.

599
00:57:42.560 --> 00:57:43.920
My diagnosis?

600
00:57:44.440 --> 00:57:45.800
It's up here.

601
00:57:48.360 --> 00:57:52.240
You say you can't sleep.
Heartbreak? Bad dreams?

602
00:57:53.400 --> 00:57:56.000
There is one dream where...

603
00:57:56.400 --> 00:57:57.800
...in my dream...

604
00:57:58.960 --> 00:58:00.240
...I'm Spider-Man.

605
00:58:00.640 --> 00:58:04.920
But I'm losing my powers.
I'm climbing a wall. but I keep falling.

606
00:58:08.440 --> 00:58:10.000
So you're Spider-Man.

607
00:58:10.160 --> 00:58:11.320
In my dream.

608
00:58:11.560 --> 00:58:15.760
Actually. it's not even my dream.
It's a friend of mine's dream.

609
00:58:17.880 --> 00:58:19.440
Somebody else's dream.

610
00:58:25.000 --> 00:58:26.800
What about this friend?

611
00:58:26.960 --> 00:58:30.160
Why does he climb these walls?
What does he think of himself?

612
00:58:30.640 --> 00:58:34.440
That's the problem.
He doesn't know what to think.

613
00:58:35.080 --> 00:58:38.680
Gotta make you mad not to know
who you are. Your soul disappears.

614
00:58:38.800 --> 00:58:40.480
Nothing as bad as uncertainty.

615
00:58:41.240 --> 00:58:42.800
Listen...

616
00:58:43.640 --> 00:58:47.720
...maybe you're not supposed to be
Spider-Man climbing those walls.

617
00:58:48.160 --> 00:58:49.800
That's why you keep falling.

618
00:58:52.200 --> 00:58:54.000
You always have a choice. Peter.

619
00:58:56.160 --> 00:58:57.800
I have a choice.

620
00:59:06.520 --> 00:59:09.400
All the things you've
been thinking about. Peter...

621
00:59:10.440 --> 00:59:11.840
...make me sad.

622
00:59:13.280 --> 00:59:15.160
Can't you understand?

623
00:59:15.840 --> 00:59:18.080
I'm in love with Mary Jane.

624
00:59:18.800 --> 00:59:21.720
Peter. all the times
we've talked of honesty...

625
00:59:22.360 --> 00:59:24.880
...fairness. justice...

626
00:59:25.600 --> 00:59:30.160
Out of those times.
I counted on you to have the courage...

627
00:59:30.400 --> 00:59:34.080
...to take those dreams
out into the world.

628
00:59:35.160 --> 00:59:37.600
I can't live your dreams anymore.

629
00:59:38.760 --> 00:59:40.480
I want a life of my own.

630
00:59:40.680 --> 00:59:42.680
You've been given a gift. Peter.

631
00:59:43.000 --> 00:59:47.040
With great power
comes great responsibility.

632
00:59:51.440 --> 00:59:53.040
Take my hand. son.

633
01:00:05.800 --> 01:00:07.360
No. Uncle Ben.

634
01:00:09.400 --> 01:00:11.560
I'm just Peter Parker.

635
01:00:13.240 --> 01:00:14.840
I'm Spider-Man...

636
01:00:15.720 --> 01:00:17.160
...no more.

637
01:00:18.320 --> 01:00:19.640
No more.

638
01:00:27.560 --> 01:00:28.960
No more.

639
01:01:54.320 --> 01:01:56.360
You punk!
Sorry.

640
01:01:57.080 --> 01:01:58.800
Thanks.
You're welcome.

641
01:02:05.960 --> 01:02:07.160
Hurry up!

642
01:02:16.440 --> 01:02:20.000
And when the borderline is tau
equals zero. the eigenvalues are...?

643
01:02:20.160 --> 01:02:21.840
Someone. please?

644
01:02:23.960 --> 01:02:26.080
23 electron voIts.

645
01:02:31.200 --> 01:02:33.920
Excellent work today. Parker.
Keep it up.

646
01:02:44.160 --> 01:02:46.960
I'm not really wicked at all.
You mustn't think that I'm wicked.

647
01:02:47.120 --> 01:02:49.840
If you are not. then you have
certainly been deceiving us all...

648
01:02:49.960 --> 01:02:51.880
...in a very inexcusable manner.

649
01:02:52.040 --> 01:02:54.120
I hope you have not been
leading a double life...

650
01:02:54.240 --> 01:02:57.320
...pretending to be wicked
and being really good all the time.

651
01:02:57.520 --> 01:02:59.240
That would be hypocrisy.

652
01:03:00.200 --> 01:03:02.480
Of course. I have been
rather reckless.

653
01:03:08.040 --> 01:03:09.480
"I am glad."

654
01:03:10.360 --> 01:03:12.280
"I am glad."

655
01:03:12.560 --> 01:03:14.240
"I am glad."

656
01:03:16.000 --> 01:03:18.040
Are you glad to hear it?

657
01:03:20.120 --> 01:03:22.400
I am glad...

658
01:03:22.600 --> 01:03:23.960
...to hear it.

659
01:03:24.160 --> 01:03:25.760
In fact. now you mention
the subject...

660
01:03:25.880 --> 01:03:29.400
...I have been very bad
in my own small way.

661
01:03:31.400 --> 01:03:33.400
You were so wonderful.
That was such a great play.

662
01:03:33.440 --> 01:03:36.400
You could've told me
you were coming.

663
01:03:36.440 --> 01:03:37.800
I was afraid you'd say.
"Don't come."

664
01:03:41.800 --> 01:03:43.280
You look different.

665
01:03:44.440 --> 01:03:48.080
I shined my shoes. pressed my pants.
did my homework.

666
01:03:49.600 --> 01:03:50.720
I do my homework now.

667
01:03:53.120 --> 01:03:54.960
You wanna get some chow mein?

668
01:03:55.000 --> 01:03:55.720
Peter...

669
01:03:56.720 --> 01:03:58.080
...I'm getting married.

670
01:04:03.120 --> 01:04:05.920
I always imagined you
getting married on a hilltop.

671
01:04:06.080 --> 01:04:07.600
And who's the groom?

672
01:04:07.680 --> 01:04:09.920
You hadn't decided yet.

673
01:04:12.080 --> 01:04:16.480
You think just because you saw my play
you can talk me out of getting married?

674
01:04:16.520 --> 01:04:19.280
You once told me you loved me.
I let things get in the way before.

675
01:04:19.320 --> 01:04:22.720
There was something I thought
I had to do. I don't have to.

676
01:04:23.840 --> 01:04:24.560
You're too late.

677
01:04:26.400 --> 01:04:27.680
Will you think about it?

678
01:04:27.720 --> 01:04:28.920
Think about what?

679
01:04:29.200 --> 01:04:30.680
Picking up where we left off.

680
01:04:31.600 --> 01:04:32.720
Where was that?

681
01:04:32.760 --> 01:04:35.280
We never got on.
You can't get off if you don't get hang Peter.

682
01:04:35.320 --> 01:04:36.640
I don't think it's that simple.

683
01:04:36.720 --> 01:04:39.240
Of course you don't.
because you complicate things.

684
01:04:39.280 --> 01:04:40.680
You don't understand.

685
01:04:41.200 --> 01:04:42.800
I'm not an empty seat anymore.

686
01:04:44.160 --> 01:04:45.480
I'm different.

687
01:04:45.920 --> 01:04:47.360
Punch me. I bleed.

688
01:04:54.920 --> 01:04:56.360
I have to go.

689
01:05:03.320 --> 01:05:05.480
I'm getting married in a church.

690
01:05:12.880 --> 01:05:14.320
You are different.

691
01:05:28.600 --> 01:05:31.600
Dear. we agreed to put on a wedding.
not go into bankruptcy.

692
01:05:32.400 --> 01:05:34.880
Caviar?
What. are we inviting the czar?

693
01:05:35.040 --> 01:05:37.920
Get some cheese and crackers.
some of those little cocktail weenies.

694
01:05:38.120 --> 01:05:41.160
I got a garbage man here says he's
got something you might want to see.

695
01:05:41.320 --> 01:05:44.720
If you have an extraterrestrial's head in
there. you're the third guy this week.

696
01:05:47.280 --> 01:05:49.040
Where the hell did you get that?

697
01:05:49.200 --> 01:05:50.680
In the garbage.

698
01:05:50.840 --> 01:05:52.200
In the garbage?

699
01:05:54.160 --> 01:05:55.840
He must've given up.

700
01:05:56.120 --> 01:06:00.680
Thrown in the towel.
Abandoned his sad little masquerade.

701
01:06:01.480 --> 01:06:04.560
I finally got to him.
The power of the press triumphs.

702
01:06:04.720 --> 01:06:09.320
Yeah. yeah. yeah. Now. look. I think
I deserve a little something for this.

703
01:06:09.520 --> 01:06:12.440
Give you 50 bucks.
I could get more than that on eBay.

704
01:06:12.600 --> 01:06:15.520
All right. 100. Give this man his
money and throw in a bar of soap.

705
01:06:16.240 --> 01:06:18.160
Your wife is still on that line.

706
01:06:19.480 --> 01:06:21.160
Flowers? How much?

707
01:06:21.800 --> 01:06:24.840
You spend any more on this thing.
you can pick the daisies off my grave.

708
01:06:25.040 --> 01:06:26.240
Get plastic.

709
01:06:27.280 --> 01:06:28.840
Gotta go. big story.

710
01:06:39.480 --> 01:06:42.600
Spider-Man
Spider-Man...

711
01:06:42.800 --> 01:06:45.640
Where have you gone to
Spider-Man?

712
01:06:45.840 --> 01:06:49.080
Where have you gone to
Spider-Man?

713
01:06:56.240 --> 01:06:58.440
Come on. man. Get the money.

714
01:07:00.080 --> 01:07:01.800
Come on. come on.

715
01:07:04.080 --> 01:07:05.520
Help!

716
01:07:09.320 --> 01:07:10.480
Come on!

717
01:07:16.720 --> 01:07:18.880
It wasn't fair to have gone like that.

718
01:07:19.040 --> 01:07:21.120
He was a peaceful man.

719
01:07:23.080 --> 01:07:25.200
And it was all my doing.

720
01:07:56.720 --> 01:08:00.000
Aunt May.
You don't have to punish yourself.

721
01:08:00.160 --> 01:08:02.080
Oh. I know I shouldn't.

722
01:08:02.480 --> 01:08:05.520
It's just that you wanted
to take the subway...

723
01:08:05.680 --> 01:08:07.760
...and he wanted to drive you.

724
01:08:08.080 --> 01:08:10.520
If only I had stopped him.

725
01:08:10.960 --> 01:08:14.000
We'd all three of us
be having tea together.

726
01:08:29.120 --> 01:08:30.560
I'm responsible.

727
01:08:34.320 --> 01:08:35.560
For what?

728
01:08:36.520 --> 01:08:38.600
For what happened to Uncle Ben.

729
01:08:38.800 --> 01:08:41.000
But you were at the library.

730
01:08:41.160 --> 01:08:43.000
You were doing your homework.

731
01:08:43.160 --> 01:08:46.160
He drove me to the library.
but I never went in.

732
01:08:46.960 --> 01:08:48.520
What do you mean?

733
01:08:49.240 --> 01:08:50.840
I went someplace else.

734
01:08:51.000 --> 01:08:53.880
Someplace where I thought
I could win some money...

735
01:08:55.000 --> 01:08:57.640
...to buy a car. because I wanted...

736
01:08:58.640 --> 01:09:00.680
...to impress Mary Jane.

737
01:09:02.760 --> 01:09:04.680
It happened so fast.

738
01:09:05.800 --> 01:09:09.480
I won the money. and the guy
wouldn't pay me. Then he got robbed.

739
01:09:10.960 --> 01:09:12.320
The thief...

740
01:09:13.280 --> 01:09:15.160
...was running towards me.

741
01:09:16.720 --> 01:09:19.400
I could've stopped him.
but I wanted...

742
01:09:20.080 --> 01:09:21.560
...revenge.

743
01:09:23.480 --> 01:09:24.960
I let him go.

744
01:09:26.800 --> 01:09:29.600
I let him get away.

745
01:09:35.200 --> 01:09:36.920
He wanted a car.

746
01:09:37.080 --> 01:09:39.240
He tried to take Uncle Ben's.

747
01:09:40.480 --> 01:09:43.560
Uncle Ben said no...

748
01:09:45.040 --> 01:09:47.080
...and then he shot him.

749
01:09:50.560 --> 01:09:54.080
Uncle Ben was killed that night...

750
01:09:55.640 --> 01:09:58.560
...for being the only one
who did the right thing.

751
01:10:01.680 --> 01:10:02.880
And I...

752
01:10:06.160 --> 01:10:08.120
I held his hand...

753
01:10:08.720 --> 01:10:10.240
...when he died.

754
01:10:17.520 --> 01:10:20.360
I've tried to tell you so many times.

755
01:11:14.640 --> 01:11:16.840
Just one more little chore.

756
01:11:24.040 --> 01:11:25.360
Where are you?

757
01:11:27.480 --> 01:11:31.160
I'm leaving for the night. sir.
Fine.

758
01:11:31.320 --> 01:11:33.960
Your father only obsessed
over his work.

759
01:11:34.120 --> 01:11:35.640
Good night. Bernard.

760
01:12:26.840 --> 01:12:28.040
Hello. Harry.

761
01:12:28.200 --> 01:12:30.320
Otto. What do you want?

762
01:12:30.920 --> 01:12:32.400
That precious tritium.

763
01:12:33.280 --> 01:12:34.880
But I need more of it this time.

764
01:12:36.560 --> 01:12:40.360
More tritium. are you crazy?
You'll destroy the city! You're a hack!

765
01:12:44.120 --> 01:12:46.000
Hey! Hey!

766
01:12:46.160 --> 01:12:49.120
Stop! Stop! All right!

767
01:12:49.520 --> 01:12:53.120
All right. all right. all right.
Put me down. We'll make a deal.

768
01:13:02.640 --> 01:13:05.760
Kill Spider-Man.
I'll give you all the tritium you need.

769
01:13:06.560 --> 01:13:10.280
On second thought.
bring him to me alive.

770
01:13:10.440 --> 01:13:11.680
How do I find him?

771
01:13:12.880 --> 01:13:14.440
Peter Parker.
Parker?

772
01:13:14.640 --> 01:13:16.840
He takes pictures of Spider-Man
for the Bugle.

773
01:13:17.040 --> 01:13:18.440
Make him tell you where he is.

774
01:13:23.960 --> 01:13:25.240
Have it ready.

775
01:13:28.880 --> 01:13:30.400
Don't hurt Peter!

776
01:13:43.080 --> 01:13:45.400
Somebody. help!

777
01:13:46.320 --> 01:13:47.840
Fire!

778
01:13:55.680 --> 01:13:58.560
Alisa. the Chens can't find their
daughter. Have you seen her?

779
01:13:59.920 --> 01:14:02.400
Somebody call the fire department!
Help!

780
01:14:03.120 --> 01:14:05.320
Help!
ls anybody in that building?

781
01:14:05.520 --> 01:14:08.000
We think there's a kid
stuck on the second floor.

782
01:14:08.240 --> 01:14:09.800
Hey. where you going?!

783
01:14:30.160 --> 01:14:31.480
I'm coming!

784
01:14:55.000 --> 01:14:57.680
It's okay. It's okay. Come here.
I'm gonna get you out of here.

785
01:14:57.840 --> 01:15:00.240
Come on. Come on.

786
01:15:58.040 --> 01:15:59.920
Mama.

787
01:16:11.440 --> 01:16:12.960
You got some guts. kid.

788
01:16:13.120 --> 01:16:17.520
Some poor soul got trapped
on the fourth floor. Never made it out.

789
01:16:17.800 --> 01:16:19.200
Oh. man.

790
01:16:22.000 --> 01:16:25.280
All right. Billy. let's knock it down
and roll them up. Get on out of here.

791
01:16:25.480 --> 01:16:29.160
Let's pick it up! Let's get all this
equipment. let's go! Let's move it!

792
01:16:34.640 --> 01:16:37.520
Am I not supposed to have
what I want?

793
01:16:38.480 --> 01:16:39.880
What I need?

794
01:16:42.160 --> 01:16:44.480
What am I supposed to do?

795
01:16:50.880 --> 01:16:52.320
I shouldn't have without...

796
01:16:52.960 --> 01:16:54.160
...knocking.

797
01:16:58.560 --> 01:17:00.080
Come in.

798
01:17:03.040 --> 01:17:05.440
Hi.
Hi.

799
01:17:08.960 --> 01:17:11.440
Would you like a piece
of chocolate cake?

800
01:17:13.360 --> 01:17:14.600
Okay.

801
01:17:16.120 --> 01:17:17.800
And a glass of milk?

802
01:17:20.720 --> 01:17:22.240
That would be nice.

803
01:17:24.120 --> 01:17:26.160
Okay.

804
01:17:45.520 --> 01:17:47.280
Thank you.

805
01:17:51.880 --> 01:17:53.360
You got a message.

806
01:17:54.480 --> 01:17:55.880
It's your aunt.

807
01:17:56.080 --> 01:17:57.760
Thanks.

808
01:18:13.200 --> 01:18:14.440
What's going on?

809
01:18:14.640 --> 01:18:18.280
Oh. they gave me another few weeks.
but I decided the hell with it.

810
01:18:18.440 --> 01:18:21.960
I'm moving on.
I found a small apartment.

811
01:18:22.160 --> 01:18:23.520
Why didn't you tell me?

812
01:18:23.680 --> 01:18:26.840
I'm quite able
to take care of things myself.

813
01:18:27.000 --> 01:18:30.280
And Henry Jackson across
the street is giving me a hand...

814
01:18:30.440 --> 01:18:31.840
...and I'm giving him $5.

815
01:18:32.040 --> 01:18:33.560
That's Henry Jackson?

816
01:18:34.200 --> 01:18:36.200
Yes. It's funny what happens
in two years.

817
01:18:36.520 --> 01:18:39.800
Nine years old. has great ambitions.

818
01:18:41.400 --> 01:18:44.440
Listen. about my last visit...

819
01:18:44.720 --> 01:18:46.960
Pish-posh. we needn't talk about it.

820
01:18:47.120 --> 01:18:51.520
It's water over the dam or under
the bridge or wherever you like it.

821
01:18:54.840 --> 01:18:58.480
But you made a brave move
in telling me the truth.

822
01:18:58.720 --> 01:19:00.520
And I'm proud of you.

823
01:19:01.520 --> 01:19:03.840
And I thank you. and l...

824
01:19:05.040 --> 01:19:07.280
I love you. Peter.

825
01:19:08.480 --> 01:19:10.880
So very. very much.

826
01:19:29.560 --> 01:19:32.440
Hey. Where are all my comic books?

827
01:19:32.600 --> 01:19:35.400
Those dreadful things?
I gave those away.

828
01:19:38.320 --> 01:19:41.440
I put the pans in the box. Mrs. Parker.
Thank you. Henry.

829
01:19:41.600 --> 01:19:43.040
Hi. Peter.
Hey. Henry.

830
01:19:43.280 --> 01:19:44.520
You're getting tall.

831
01:19:44.720 --> 01:19:48.640
Henry. why don't you put those
cookbooks in with the mixer.

832
01:19:48.800 --> 01:19:51.760
Okay. You take
Spider-Man's pictures. right?

833
01:19:52.640 --> 01:19:53.880
I used to.

834
01:19:54.040 --> 01:19:55.240
Where is he?

835
01:19:55.400 --> 01:19:59.560
Henry and I agree. We don't see
his picture in the paper anymore.

836
01:20:01.360 --> 01:20:02.840
He...

837
01:20:04.880 --> 01:20:07.240
...quit.
Why?

838
01:20:08.080 --> 01:20:09.920
Wanted to try other things.

839
01:20:10.080 --> 01:20:11.560
He'll be back. right?

840
01:20:12.880 --> 01:20:14.080
I don't know.

841
01:20:15.440 --> 01:20:18.320
You'll never guess
who he wants to be.

842
01:20:18.720 --> 01:20:20.400
Spider-Man.

843
01:20:20.560 --> 01:20:24.320
Why?
He knows a hero when he sees one.

844
01:20:24.480 --> 01:20:28.040
Too few characters out there.
flying around like that...

845
01:20:28.240 --> 01:20:30.160
...saving old girls like me.

846
01:20:30.320 --> 01:20:33.960
And Lord knows.
kids like Henry need a hero.

847
01:20:34.160 --> 01:20:36.880
Courageous. self-sacrificing people...

848
01:20:37.040 --> 01:20:39.280
...setting examples for all of us.

849
01:20:39.760 --> 01:20:41.960
Everybody loves a hero.

850
01:20:42.320 --> 01:20:45.640
People line up for them.
Cheer them. Scream their names.

851
01:20:45.800 --> 01:20:49.800
And years later. they'll tell how
they stood in the rain for hours...

852
01:20:49.960 --> 01:20:51.560
...just to get a glimpse of the one...

853
01:20:51.760 --> 01:20:55.040
...who taught them to hold on
a second longer.

854
01:20:56.360 --> 01:20:59.440
I believe there's a hero in all of us...

855
01:21:00.200 --> 01:21:01.960
...that keeps us honest...

856
01:21:02.600 --> 01:21:04.080
...gives us strength...

857
01:21:04.520 --> 01:21:06.280
...makes us noble...

858
01:21:07.360 --> 01:21:10.720
...and finally allows us to die
with pride.

859
01:21:11.880 --> 01:21:15.840
Even though sometimes
we have to be steady...

860
01:21:16.000 --> 01:21:18.640
...and give up the thing
we want the most.

861
01:21:20.360 --> 01:21:22.160
Even our dreams.

862
01:21:24.000 --> 01:21:26.600
Spider-Man did that for Henry...

863
01:21:26.800 --> 01:21:29.120
...and he wonders where he's gone.

864
01:21:30.240 --> 01:21:31.960
He needs him.

865
01:21:36.240 --> 01:21:40.800
Do you think you could lift that desk
and put it into the garage for me?

866
01:21:41.200 --> 01:21:43.320
But don't strain yourself.

867
01:21:43.480 --> 01:21:45.040
Okay.

868
01:22:03.000 --> 01:22:05.160
Strong focus on what I want.

869
01:22:33.960 --> 01:22:35.440
I'm back!

870
01:22:35.600 --> 01:22:36.960
I'm back!

871
01:22:53.840 --> 01:22:55.160
My back.

872
01:22:56.080 --> 01:22:57.360
My back.

873
01:23:20.560 --> 01:23:24.680
Honey. you sure you don't want to
invite your friend. the photographer?

874
01:23:25.200 --> 01:23:26.440
Peter Parker?

875
01:23:28.520 --> 01:23:29.680
Positive.

876
01:23:29.920 --> 01:23:31.080
Thought he was your pal.

877
01:23:31.440 --> 01:23:33.640
Peter Parker?
Yeah.

878
01:23:34.520 --> 01:23:37.000
He's just a great big jerk.

879
01:23:37.280 --> 01:23:39.080
The world's full of great big jerks.

880
01:23:40.520 --> 01:23:42.200
You're adorable.

881
01:23:42.600 --> 01:23:44.120
It's just the uniform.

882
01:23:47.280 --> 01:23:49.320
Lean your head back for me.

883
01:23:49.600 --> 01:23:51.920
Put my head back?
Yeah. just do it.

884
01:23:53.880 --> 01:23:55.480
Just put my head back?

885
01:23:56.200 --> 01:23:57.720
Okay.

886
01:24:16.040 --> 01:24:17.440
Wow.

887
01:24:18.200 --> 01:24:19.880
I'm back on the moon.

888
01:24:24.360 --> 01:24:25.760
You up there with me?

889
01:24:45.720 --> 01:24:47.800
Hiya.
Surprised?

890
01:24:47.960 --> 01:24:49.400
Very.

891
01:24:49.560 --> 01:24:51.040
Thanks for coming.

892
01:24:51.400 --> 01:24:53.240
Everything okay?

893
01:24:54.200 --> 01:24:55.880
You might say so.

894
01:24:57.160 --> 01:25:00.760
This is funny.
I'm not sure how to begin.

895
01:25:03.120 --> 01:25:05.600
You know how our minds
play tricks on us.

896
01:25:06.040 --> 01:25:09.800
Tell me about it.
Well. mine did a real number on me.

897
01:25:11.320 --> 01:25:14.840
Some part of me heard what you
had to say after the show that night...

898
01:25:15.000 --> 01:25:18.400
...that you were different.
But I didn't want to listen.

899
01:25:19.280 --> 01:25:21.160
I was afraid to trust you.

900
01:25:22.800 --> 01:25:25.680
But I've been thinking about it...

901
01:25:25.840 --> 01:25:29.360
Listen. there's more for me to say.

902
01:25:32.880 --> 01:25:36.920
I maybe rushed into things.
I thought...

903
01:25:37.080 --> 01:25:39.600
Wait a minute.
What are you saying?

904
01:25:40.280 --> 01:25:42.000
I'm saying...

905
01:25:47.920 --> 01:25:50.800
I thought I could be there for you.
Mary Jane...

906
01:25:51.320 --> 01:25:52.720
...but I can't.

907
01:25:56.040 --> 01:25:59.120
My mind was playing tricks too.

908
01:26:03.640 --> 01:26:06.120
Do you love me. or not?

909
01:26:12.880 --> 01:26:14.440
I...

910
01:26:17.560 --> 01:26:18.760
...don't.

911
01:26:23.440 --> 01:26:25.320
You don't.

912
01:26:34.480 --> 01:26:35.640
Kiss me.

913
01:26:37.760 --> 01:26:39.200
Kiss you?

914
01:26:39.360 --> 01:26:41.120
I need to know something.

915
01:26:43.600 --> 01:26:45.120
Just one kiss.

916
01:27:30.320 --> 01:27:32.400
What's happening?

917
01:27:42.240 --> 01:27:43.800
Peter Parker...

918
01:27:44.640 --> 01:27:46.240
...and the girlfriend.

919
01:27:46.640 --> 01:27:48.400
What do you want?

920
01:27:51.120 --> 01:27:53.240
I want you to find your friend
Spider-Man.

921
01:27:53.400 --> 01:27:55.920
Tell him to meet me
at the Westside Tower at 3:00.

922
01:27:56.080 --> 01:27:58.160
I don't know where he is.

923
01:27:59.640 --> 01:28:01.080
Find him.

924
01:28:03.280 --> 01:28:06.000
Or I'll peel the flesh off her bones.

925
01:28:06.160 --> 01:28:08.120
If you lay one finger on her...

926
01:28:08.280 --> 01:28:09.560
You'll do what?

927
01:29:20.280 --> 01:29:23.880
Still no word on the whereabouts
of your son's fiancee.

928
01:29:24.040 --> 01:29:25.560
Sorry. Jonah.

929
01:29:26.600 --> 01:29:28.000
It's all my fauIt.

930
01:29:29.720 --> 01:29:31.960
I drove Spider-Man away.

931
01:29:32.240 --> 01:29:35.240
He was the only one who could've
stopped Octavius.

932
01:29:36.720 --> 01:29:37.880
Yes.

933
01:29:39.400 --> 01:29:42.600
Spider-Man was a hero.

934
01:29:43.760 --> 01:29:45.640
I just couldn't see it.

935
01:29:47.160 --> 01:29:48.520
He was a...

936
01:29:48.720 --> 01:29:51.240
A thief! A criminal!

937
01:29:52.760 --> 01:29:54.960
He stole my suit!
He's a menace to the entire city!

938
01:29:55.120 --> 01:29:58.040
I want that wall-crawling
arachnid prosecuted!

939
01:29:58.200 --> 01:30:00.200
I want him strung up by his web!

940
01:30:01.680 --> 01:30:04.200
I want Spider-Man!

941
01:30:31.520 --> 01:30:32.840
Where is she?

942
01:30:33.000 --> 01:30:35.520
Oh. she'll be just fine. Let's talk.

943
01:31:24.640 --> 01:31:25.800
What the hell?

944
01:33:25.680 --> 01:33:27.640
You have a train to catch.

945
01:33:30.040 --> 01:33:31.800
Help!

946
01:33:31.960 --> 01:33:36.160
Help! Help! I can't stop it!
The brakes are gone!

947
01:33:54.160 --> 01:33:56.600
It's Spider-Man.
Oh. my God. this is it!

948
01:33:56.760 --> 01:33:58.240
Tell everyone to hang on!

949
01:33:58.400 --> 01:34:00.040
Brace yourselves!

950
01:34:20.400 --> 01:34:22.600
Any more bright ideas?

951
01:34:22.960 --> 01:34:25.200
I got a few. yeah!

952
01:34:45.680 --> 01:34:47.400
Whoa. watch out!

953
01:35:16.800 --> 01:35:18.000
We're slowing down.

954
01:36:19.760 --> 01:36:21.640
Nice and easy. we'll go down.

955
01:36:22.600 --> 01:36:24.040
Slower. Gently.

956
01:36:29.080 --> 01:36:30.360
Is he alive?

957
01:36:34.000 --> 01:36:35.160
He's...

958
01:36:35.320 --> 01:36:36.840
...just a kid.

959
01:36:37.960 --> 01:36:39.720
No older than my son.

960
01:36:58.280 --> 01:37:00.040
It's all right.

961
01:37:04.240 --> 01:37:06.000
We found something.

962
01:37:15.000 --> 01:37:16.960
We won't tell nobody.

963
01:37:30.080 --> 01:37:32.480
It's good to have you back.
Spider-Man.

964
01:37:51.680 --> 01:37:53.440
He's mine!

965
01:37:54.200 --> 01:37:56.840
You want to get to him.
you got to go through me.

966
01:37:57.160 --> 01:37:58.440
And me.

967
01:37:59.000 --> 01:38:00.320
Me too.

968
01:38:05.040 --> 01:38:06.560
Very well.

969
01:38:34.360 --> 01:38:36.240
Where do you want him?

970
01:38:43.720 --> 01:38:45.160
And the tritium?

971
01:38:59.080 --> 01:39:00.520
Yes.

972
01:39:29.320 --> 01:39:32.240
If only I could cause you the pain
that you've caused me.

973
01:39:34.880 --> 01:39:37.280
First we'll see who's behind the mask.

974
01:39:37.480 --> 01:39:39.800
I can look into your eyes as you die.

975
01:39:42.440 --> 01:39:43.920
Pete.

976
01:39:44.280 --> 01:39:45.920
No.

977
01:39:46.480 --> 01:39:47.840
It can't be.

978
01:39:54.120 --> 01:39:55.400
Harry.

979
01:39:56.840 --> 01:40:00.160
Where is she?
Where is he keeping her?

980
01:40:01.440 --> 01:40:05.280
He's got M.J.
No. All he wanted was the tritium.

981
01:40:05.960 --> 01:40:07.200
Tritium?

982
01:40:09.120 --> 01:40:11.040
He's making the machine again.

983
01:40:11.840 --> 01:40:15.880
When that happens. she'll die.
along with half of New York.

984
01:40:16.040 --> 01:40:18.720
Now. where is he?
Peter...

985
01:40:19.840 --> 01:40:21.600
...you killed my father.

986
01:40:26.560 --> 01:40:30.480
There are bigger things
happening here than me and you.

987
01:40:31.200 --> 01:40:33.840
Harry. please. I've got to stop him.

988
01:40:44.040 --> 01:40:45.640
Hey!

989
01:40:46.680 --> 01:40:48.280
Hey!

990
01:40:49.640 --> 01:40:51.320
I'm talking to you!

991
01:40:51.640 --> 01:40:55.000
You got what you needed for your little
science project. now let me go.

992
01:40:55.160 --> 01:40:56.960
I can't let you go.
you'd bring the police.

993
01:40:57.120 --> 01:40:59.560
Not that anybody could stop me
now that Spider-Man's dead.

994
01:41:00.520 --> 01:41:01.880
He's not dead.

995
01:41:02.120 --> 01:41:04.640
I don't believe you.
Believe it.

996
01:41:21.680 --> 01:41:22.960
Surprise.

997
01:41:27.240 --> 01:41:28.800
As soon as you get free...

998
01:41:30.880 --> 01:41:34.680
I should have known Osborn
wouldn't have the spine to finish you!

999
01:41:34.840 --> 01:41:37.760
Shut it down. Ock. You're going
to hurt a lot more people this time.

1000
01:41:37.960 --> 01:41:40.200
Well. that's a risk
we're willing to take.

1001
01:41:41.320 --> 01:41:43.080
Well. I'm not.

1002
01:42:14.280 --> 01:42:15.480
Hang on. Mary Jane!

1003
01:42:30.760 --> 01:42:31.960
Run!

1004
01:42:55.520 --> 01:42:57.760
Let's see you scurry out of this.

1005
01:43:20.640 --> 01:43:22.760
Now what?

1006
01:43:51.640 --> 01:43:53.680
Dr. Octavius.

1007
01:43:56.760 --> 01:43:57.960
We have to shut it down.

1008
01:43:58.760 --> 01:44:00.240
Please tell me how.

1009
01:44:00.400 --> 01:44:01.800
Peter Parker?

1010
01:44:05.200 --> 01:44:07.160
"Brilliant but lazy."

1011
01:44:07.480 --> 01:44:08.840
Look at what's happening.

1012
01:44:09.800 --> 01:44:11.560
We must destroy it.

1013
01:44:17.000 --> 01:44:18.520
I can't destroy it.

1014
01:44:23.560 --> 01:44:24.840
I won't.

1015
01:44:30.200 --> 01:44:32.320
You once spoke to me
about intelligence.

1016
01:44:34.120 --> 01:44:37.640
That it was a gift to be used
for the good of mankind.

1017
01:44:39.280 --> 01:44:40.640
A privilege.

1018
01:44:41.280 --> 01:44:44.200
These things have turned you
into something you're not.

1019
01:44:45.200 --> 01:44:47.000
Don't listen to them.

1020
01:44:52.640 --> 01:44:54.120
It was my dream.

1021
01:44:54.280 --> 01:44:58.600
Sometimes. to do what's right.
we have to be steady...

1022
01:44:58.760 --> 01:45:01.200
...and give up the thing
we want the most.

1023
01:45:01.960 --> 01:45:03.560
Even our dreams.

1024
01:45:09.320 --> 01:45:10.920
You're right.

1025
01:45:18.000 --> 01:45:19.800
He's right.

1026
01:45:21.480 --> 01:45:23.000
Listen.

1027
01:45:25.120 --> 01:45:27.280
Listen to me now.

1028
01:45:30.080 --> 01:45:32.320
Listen to me now.

1029
01:45:35.880 --> 01:45:38.720
Now. tell me how to stop it.

1030
01:45:39.760 --> 01:45:41.360
It can't be stopped.

1031
01:45:42.720 --> 01:45:44.640
It's self-sustaining now.

1032
01:45:44.880 --> 01:45:46.880
Think!
Unless...

1033
01:45:48.360 --> 01:45:50.040
The river.

1034
01:45:51.360 --> 01:45:52.880
Drown it.

1035
01:45:54.760 --> 01:45:56.040
I'll do it.

1036
01:46:39.520 --> 01:46:42.120
No!

1037
01:46:53.640 --> 01:46:55.200
Hi.

1038
01:46:55.840 --> 01:46:57.400
Hi.

1039
01:46:58.160 --> 01:46:59.560
This is really heavy.

1040
01:47:23.120 --> 01:47:25.000
M.J.

1041
01:47:25.800 --> 01:47:27.560
In case we die...

1042
01:47:27.720 --> 01:47:29.200
You do love me.

1043
01:47:29.800 --> 01:47:30.960
I do.

1044
01:47:31.880 --> 01:47:33.920
Even though you said you didn't.

1045
01:47:36.680 --> 01:47:39.080
I will not die a monster.

1046
01:48:41.640 --> 01:48:43.600
I think I always knew...

1047
01:48:44.640 --> 01:48:46.200
...all this time...

1048
01:48:47.320 --> 01:48:49.040
...who you really were.

1049
01:48:49.640 --> 01:48:52.080
Then you know
why we can't be together.

1050
01:48:53.240 --> 01:48:56.000
Spider-Man will always have enemies.

1051
01:48:57.840 --> 01:49:00.440
I can't let you take that risk.

1052
01:49:04.960 --> 01:49:06.280
I will...

1053
01:49:07.880 --> 01:49:10.040
...always be Spider-Man.

1054
01:49:12.680 --> 01:49:14.960
You and I can never be.

1055
01:50:01.360 --> 01:50:03.280
Mary Jane!

1056
01:51:03.800 --> 01:51:05.400
Hello?

1057
01:51:20.760 --> 01:51:22.040
Who's that?

1058
01:51:22.200 --> 01:51:24.040
Son.

1059
01:51:25.120 --> 01:51:26.400
I'm here.

1060
01:51:27.680 --> 01:51:29.240
Dad?

1061
01:51:30.280 --> 01:51:32.360
I thought you were...
No.

1062
01:51:32.840 --> 01:51:34.880
I'm alive in you. Harry.

1063
01:51:35.040 --> 01:51:36.200
Now it's your turn.

1064
01:51:37.720 --> 01:51:40.280
You swore to make Spider-Man pay.

1065
01:51:40.640 --> 01:51:42.240
Now make him pay.

1066
01:51:42.720 --> 01:51:44.280
But Pete's my best friend.

1067
01:51:44.520 --> 01:51:45.920
And I'm your father.

1068
01:51:46.920 --> 01:51:48.280
You're weak.

1069
01:51:49.240 --> 01:51:53.400
You were always weak. You'll always
be weak until you take control.

1070
01:51:54.440 --> 01:51:57.160
Now you know the truth about Peter.

1071
01:51:58.040 --> 01:51:59.480
Be strong. Harry.

1072
01:52:00.480 --> 01:52:01.800
Avenge me.

1073
01:52:04.520 --> 01:52:06.480
Avenge me!
No!

1074
01:54:25.200 --> 01:54:26.560
Call Deborah.

1075
01:54:26.720 --> 01:54:28.480
The caterer?

1076
01:54:29.440 --> 01:54:31.440
Tell her not to open the caviar.

1077
01:55:11.120 --> 01:55:13.200
Had to do what I had to do.

1078
01:55:14.800 --> 01:55:16.080
Mary Jane.

1079
01:55:17.200 --> 01:55:18.440
Peter.

1080
01:55:19.600 --> 01:55:21.960
I can't survive without you.

1081
01:55:31.560 --> 01:55:33.320
You shouldn't be here.

1082
01:55:34.360 --> 01:55:37.280
I know you think we can't be together.

1083
01:55:38.360 --> 01:55:41.880
But can't you respect me enough
to let me make my own decision?

1084
01:55:43.080 --> 01:55:44.840
I know there'll be risks.

1085
01:55:45.640 --> 01:55:48.120
But I want to face them with you.

1086
01:55:49.240 --> 01:55:52.480
It's wrong that
we should only be half-alive...

1087
01:55:52.640 --> 01:55:54.320
...half of ourselves.

1088
01:55:56.680 --> 01:55:58.240
I love you.

1089
01:56:00.440 --> 01:56:03.240
So here I am.
standing in your doorway.

1090
01:56:04.920 --> 01:56:07.880
I've always been
standing in your doorway.

1091
01:56:14.640 --> 01:56:18.040
Isn't it about time somebody
saved your life?

1092
01:56:23.720 --> 01:56:25.480
Well. say something.

1093
01:56:27.880 --> 01:56:30.280
Thank you. Mary Jane Watson.

1094
01:56:45.800 --> 01:56:47.520
Go get them. tiger.

